All 7 tests remain green. Rule 3 (duplication): the `"rune"` literal appears in both filters; extracting an `isRune` predicate would remove it but adds an element for marginal gain at this stage — declined per Rule 4. Rule 4: no unnecessary abstractions; the `as QuoteStep` cast in `runScenario` is the minimal shape the 7 active tests demand.

Final file state for reference — `/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-09-10_19-13-08_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.1-hybrid-testlist-scope-fix_fable-5-no-thinking-2/src/claim-office.ts`, `quotePremium` now reads:

```typescript
const RUNE_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;
const RUNE_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;

const quotePremium = (items: QuoteItem[]): number => {
  const runeCount = items.filter((item) => item.type === "rune").length;
  const runesPremium =
    runeCount === RUNE_BLOCK_SIZE
      ? RUNE_BLOCK_PREMIUM
      : runeCount * BASE_PREMIUMS.rune;
  const otherItemsPremium = items
    .filter((item) => item.type !== "rune")
    .reduce((sum, item) => sum + BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type], 0);
  const policyBasePremium = runesPremium + otherItemsPremium;
  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBasePremium / 10;
  return policyBasePremium + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE;
};
```

**Refactoring Applied**:
- Naming: `quotePremium`, `runScenario` still fit; renamed `runePremium` → `runesPremium` (it is the group premium, not per-rune)
- Rule 2: extracted magic numbers into `RUNE_BLOCK_SIZE` / `RUNE_BLOCK_PREMIUM`; un-hid the rune premium from the reduce seed so the composition `policyBasePremium = runesPremium + otherItemsPremium` is explicit
- Rule 3: evaluated `"rune"` literal duplication; extraction declined (adds an element, minimal gain)
- Rule 4: nothing to remove

**Mass Change**: 52 → 57 (Δ +5: one extra binding, seed constant, and `+`). Deliberate — Rule 2 (reveals intent) trumps APP; the seeded-reduce trick was the least readable part of the function.

🔄 Refactor Phase Complete:
**Refactoring**: named block constants, explicit premium composition, `runesPremium` rename
